hanged its name to TotalEnergies SE in June 2021. TotalEnergies SE was incorporated in 1924 and is headquartered in Courbevoie, France.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Patrick  Pouyanne | Chairman & CEO | Age 62 | Compensation: $4.7M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 94K people. Revenue per employee of $2.1M ranks in the above the sector median among Energy peers. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["TotalEnergies SE is a large-cap energy business with a $186.6B market cap on $201.2B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -11% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 8% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","On the balance sheet, interest coverage runs at 8.3\u00d7.","Management returns a meaningful 8.7% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 8.9% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.3) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Priced near or above estimated fair value, so the margin of safety has been bid away","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.05442651986536051},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Energy peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"News sentiment running negative (-0.13) across recent coverage","sev":"amber","cat":"news"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Energy ten